# Sentiment Analysis using Machine Learning

## Objective
Build a machine learning model that classifies text into Positive, Negative, and Neutral sentiments.

## Tech Stack
- Python
- Pandas
- Scikit-learn
- NLTK
- Matplotlib
- WordCloud
- Jupyter Notebook

## Features
- Load dataset
- Data preprocessing
- TF-IDF Vectorizer
- Train/Test Split
- Naive Bayes Classifier
- Logistic Regression Classifier
- Accuracy, Precision, Recall, F1-score
- Confusion Matrix
- Sentiment Distribution Chart
- WordCloud
- Error Analysis
- Conclusion

## Models Used
1. Multinomial Naive Bayes
2. Logistic Regression

## Results
Logistic Regression performed better than Naive Bayes for sentiment classification.

## Applications
- Customer Feedback Analysis
- Product Review Analysis
- Social Media Monitoring
- Brand Reputation Analysis
